// A key combination the desktop claims for itself.
//
// The same shape `DomicileShortcutEvent` hands back, so a shell writes the
// combination once and compares against the press with the same field names.
//
// `keycode` rather than `key`: this is a Linux evdev code, and `KeyboardEvent`
// already spends `key` on a string ("Enter"). The modifiers keep the web's
// names, so a shell that already reads `event.ctrlKey` reads this the same way.
dictionary DomicileShortcut {
  required unsigned long keycode;
  boolean altKey = false;
  boolean ctrlKey = false;
  boolean shiftKey = false;
  boolean metaKey = false;
};
